  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "Two  parallel lines; compare 一 (one) and 三 (three)"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Two horizontal strokes, representing the number two."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "地之數也。从偶一。凡二之屬皆从二。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Ideogram (指事) - two parallel strokes. Compare with 一, one stroke meaning one, 三, three strokes meaning three, and 亖 (sǐ), four strokes meaning four. Duplication of 一 (“one”).\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *kV-ni-s. Cognate to Tibetan གཉིས (gnyis), Sikkimese ཉི (nyi), Tangut 𗍫 (*njɨ̱¹), Burmese နှစ် (hnac), and Nuosu ꑍ (nyip). See also: 次 (OC *sn̥ʰis, “second; next”), a cognate within Chinese languages."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "地之數也。从偶一。凡二之屬皆从二。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "數 of earth. Composed with 偶一. All characters in the 二 category contain 二 as radical.",
